<title>USA: Dow opens lower after July jobs data.</title>
<headline>Dow opens lower after July jobs data.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. blue chip stocks opened lower on  Friday, after the release of July employment data which showed an  above-forecast gain in nonfarm payrolls and a decline in the jobless  rate to 4.8 percent.</p>
<p>The Dow Industrials index was off 5.11 at 8217.50, while the 30-year  long bond off 17/32 at 6.34 percent yield.</p>
</text>
